// A 4 KiB initializer (sea.mem.fill of 4096 bytes): the expansion makes one
// store per byte (4096), and the array VC of the lowered program is built
// (query size, docs/design/MemFill.md: about 17k DAG nodes; lambda memory
// takes about 23 s to build it, a quadratic simplification of long store
// chains, so it is not run here).
// RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/mem-fill-4k.py > %t/fill4k.mlir
// RUN: sea-opt %t/fill4k.mlir --sea-expand-mem-fill | grep -c 'sea.store' | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STORES
// RUN: sea-vc %t/fill4k.mlir --lower --vcgen-only --dag-stats | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VC
// STORES: 4096
// VC: vc.dag-size:

